1
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:05,120
So, anyway, last night on video chat,

2
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:08,500
I spent, like, 20 minutes just staring into Lucy's eyes.

3
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:09,730
Oh, that sounds romantic.

4
00:00:09,730 --> 00:00:12,410
It was until I realized the screen had frozen.

5
00:00:13,310 --> 00:00:15,840
Still one of my top three dates of all time.

6
00:00:16,380 --> 00:00:18,690
So, are we ever gonna hang out with this girl?

7
00:00:18,690 --> 00:00:19,560
I'd love that,

8
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:21,920
but she's not really comfortable around people.

9
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:24,760
Yeah, I used to be uncomfortable around people,

10
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:26,400
but then I learned a trick.

11
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,240
I pretend everyone I meet

12
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:31,420
is a beloved character from Star Trek.

13
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:34,050
How's that been working for you?

14
00:00:34,050 --> 00:00:37,550
Oh, like a charm, unnamed crewman in a red shirt.

15
00:00:37,550 --> 00:00:41,810
Leonard, I may have gotten you a job.

16
00:00:41,810 --> 00:00:43,610
- I have a job. - Yes, he does.

17
00:00:43,610 --> 00:00:45,750
He caters to my every whim.

18
00:00:46,850 --> 00:00:50,120
No, in a couple of weeks, Stephen Hawking's team

19
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:51,680
is sending an expedition to the North Sea

20
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:54,270
to test hydrodynamic simulations of black holes.

21
00:00:54,270 --> 00:00:56,750
One of their experimental physicists dropped out,

22
00:00:56,750 --> 00:00:58,890
and I recommended you.

23
00:00:59,470 --> 00:01:01,110
Well, do you really think I have a shot?

24
00:01:01,110 --> 00:01:03,430
Yeah, I've worked with Hawking. I talked you up.

25
00:01:03,430 --> 00:01:04,870
He knows your research.

26
00:01:04,870 --> 00:01:06,280
I think this could happen.

27
00:01:06,280 --> 00:01:08,400
He knows-- Wow!

28
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:11,820
Well, now, but do you think that's a good idea?

29
00:01:12,710 --> 00:01:14,670
I do. Uh, you know Star Trek.

30
00:01:14,670 --> 00:01:16,350
Should a guy with no name

31
00:01:16,350 --> 00:01:19,280
and a red shirt really go on an expedition?

32
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:21,540
Hey, don't discourage him.

33
00:01:21,540 --> 00:01:23,230
This is a fantastic opportunity.

34
00:01:23,230 --> 00:01:25,250
No one asked you, Uhura.

35
00:01:29,390 --> 00:01:33,320
Would you like to hear a classic Sheldon Cooper factoid?

36
00:01:33,320 --> 00:01:35,670
- What do you think? - Great.

37
00:01:36,830 --> 00:01:40,330
I've been doing some reading about vehicular safety.

38
00:01:40,330 --> 00:01:42,980
Did you know that the highest number

39
00:01:42,980 --> 00:01:47,800
of drowning accidents happen on or around boats?

40
00:01:48,450 --> 00:01:50,820
Interesting that you would bring that up

41
00:01:50,820 --> 00:01:52,670
when I might go work on a boat.

42
00:01:52,670 --> 00:01:54,290
Well, that's the thing about factoids--

43
00:01:54,290 --> 00:01:56,100
they're interesting.

44
00:01:57,830 --> 00:01:59,130
I know what you're doing.

45
00:01:59,850 --> 00:02:01,700
You don't want me going on this research trip

46
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:03,770
because you're afraid to be alone.

47
00:02:03,770 --> 00:02:05,970
I'm not afraid to be alone.

48
00:02:05,980 --> 00:02:07,560
On land.

49
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:11,640
On the sea, it would be terrifying.

50
00:02:13,280 --> 00:02:15,900
Because of all the drowning.

51
00:02:16,940 --> 00:02:18,080
Sheldon.

52
00:02:18,080 --> 00:02:19,680
Fine, no more drowning talk.

53
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:21,450
I'll change the subject.

54
00:02:22,140 --> 00:02:25,160
Who do you think would win in a fight--

55
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:28,560
you or a shark?

56
00:02:29,050 --> 00:02:31,840
Look, I appreciate your signature blend

57
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:35,260
of concern for me and incredible selfishness.

58
00:02:35,490 --> 00:02:36,880
If I get the chance to do this,

59
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:39,890
there is nothing you can say that's going to stop me.

60
00:02:40,530 --> 00:02:41,950
Very well.

61
00:02:43,740 --> 00:02:46,410
Things between you and Penny have never been better.

62
00:02:46,410 --> 00:02:49,750
I hope four months apart doesn't change anything.

63
00:02:54,540 --> 00:02:56,670
I should have opened with that, huh?

64
00:03:23,990 --> 00:03:26,100
If you look carefully at Venus,

65
00:03:26,100 --> 00:03:27,160
you should be able to see

66
00:03:27,160 --> 00:03:30,300
the International Space Station pass by.

67
00:03:31,730 --> 00:03:33,550
Your friend was actually up there?

68
00:03:33,550 --> 00:03:36,060
Yeah. He brought me back a T-shirt that said,

69
00:03:36,060 --> 00:03:37,350
"My Friend Went to the Space Station

70
00:03:37,350 --> 00:03:40,210
and All I Got Was This Lousy T-Shirt""

71
00:03:41,290 --> 00:03:43,330
- Did he take the T-shirt to space? - Nope.

72
00:03:43,330 --> 00:03:45,920
It's exactly as lousy as advertised.

73
00:03:47,450 --> 00:03:49,260
Speaking of friends,

74
00:03:49,260 --> 00:03:51,180
they have been asking to meet you.

75
00:03:51,930 --> 00:03:52,690
I was thinking

76
00:03:52,690 --> 00:03:54,580
maybe we could all hang out sometime?

77
00:03:55,110 --> 00:03:55,870
I don't know.

78
00:03:55,870 --> 00:03:57,240
How many are there?

79
00:03:57,240 --> 00:03:59,450
Let's see. Six.

80
00:03:59,450 --> 00:04:02,240
That's pretty cool; I have six friends!

81
00:04:03,900 --> 00:04:05,780
Kind of like Sinatra.

82
00:04:07,770 --> 00:04:09,140
Six strangers?

83
00:04:09,140 --> 00:04:10,740
That's a lot of pressure.

84
00:04:10,740 --> 00:04:13,560
Staring at me, asking me personal questions.

85
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:15,480
Like, "What do you do?"

86
00:04:15,480 --> 00:04:16,940
"Where are you from?"

87
00:04:16,940 --> 00:04:19,860
"Why did you lock yourself in the bathroom?"

88
00:04:20,320 --> 00:04:23,480
Okay, how about you just dip your toe in

89
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:24,960
and meet one of them?

90
00:04:25,990 --> 00:04:27,410
Will you be there?

91
00:04:27,410 --> 00:04:28,530
Of course.

92
00:04:28,530 --> 00:04:30,720
Well, that's two. Three if you count me.

93
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:32,490
Oh, this is getting out of hand.

94
00:04:34,750 --> 00:04:36,710
So, then, during my afternoon shift,

95
00:04:36,710 --> 00:04:39,620
I spilled an entire tray of drinks on myself.

96
00:04:39,620 --> 00:04:40,740
Oh, that's awful.

97
00:04:40,740 --> 00:04:42,490
Not really. My shirt was soaking wet.

98
00:04:42,490 --> 00:04:45,190
I got, like, the biggest tip of my life. Oh.

99
00:04:47,300 --> 00:04:49,880
So, listen, do you remember when I said

100
00:04:49,880 --> 00:04:51,420
the similarities of the equations

101
00:04:51,420 --> 00:04:54,020
of general relativity and hydrodynamics suggest

102
00:04:54,020 --> 00:04:56,810
you could find the equivalent of Unruh radiation

103
00:04:56,810 --> 00:04:58,580
in a large body of water?

104
00:04:58,580 --> 00:05:00,810
I thought I said that to you.

105
00:05:05,410 --> 00:05:06,360
Anyway,

106
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:08,680
Stephen Hawking's team is looking into that,

107
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:11,130
and I've been invited to join them.

108
00:05:11,130 --> 00:05:13,580
Wow, Hawking! Good for you!

109
00:05:13,820 --> 00:05:14,570
Well, it is.

110
00:05:14,570 --> 00:05:17,050
Just-- you know, I'd be gone for a while.

111
00:05:17,050 --> 00:05:18,170
Well, how long?

112
00:05:18,170 --> 00:05:19,390
Three, four months.

113
00:05:21,510 --> 00:05:24,050
- When would you leave? - Couple weeks.

114
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:27,530
O-Okay, well, I'll just come visit you.

115
00:05:27,530 --> 00:05:29,610
That's the thing-- you can't.

116
00:05:29,620 --> 00:05:31,550
I'll be on a ship in the North Sea.

117
00:05:31,550 --> 00:05:32,350
On a ship?

118
00:05:32,350 --> 00:05:35,190
Aren't they afraid Hawking will just roll overboard?

119
00:05:37,770 --> 00:05:38,840
Uh, he's not gonna be there.

120
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:41,920
He's just sending a team to research his theory.

121
00:05:41,920 --> 00:05:42,850
Oh, sure.

122
00:05:42,850 --> 00:05:46,150
Like when you send me to kill spiders in your bathtub.

123
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:52,370
Okay. Four months.

124
00:05:52,370 --> 00:05:53,840
Yeah.

125
00:05:53,840 --> 00:05:55,390
And I'm a little worried

126
00:05:55,390 --> 00:05:58,010
because things between us have been so great,

127
00:05:58,010 --> 00:06:00,760
and I'd hate to do anything that screws that up.

128
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:02,760
Oh, sweetie, if you're gonna screw things up,

129
00:06:02,770 --> 00:06:05,190
it's gonna be while you're here, not while you're away.

130
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:12,260
No. I mean, look, you have to go.

131
00:06:12,260 --> 00:06:14,070
It sounds like an amazing opportunity.

132
00:06:14,070 --> 00:06:15,560
And I'm just basing that on how much

133
00:06:15,560 --> 00:06:17,870
I didn't understand what you said about it.

134
00:06:19,450 --> 00:06:20,790
Okay.

135
00:06:20,790 --> 00:06:23,240
I'll confirm the travel arrangements in the morning.

136
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:25,200
Okay. Good.

137
00:06:25,960 --> 00:06:28,170
- I do have to ask you one favor. - Sure.

138
00:06:28,490 --> 00:06:29,810
Sheldon's nervous about me leaving.

139
00:06:29,810 --> 00:06:31,600
Just keep an eye on him while I'm gone.

140
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:33,310
Oh, I don't know.

141
00:06:33,310 --> 00:06:35,980
Remember what happened when I took care of your goldfish?

142
00:06:37,580 --> 00:06:40,330
Well, flush Sheldon down the toilet and get me a new one.

143
00:06:43,610 --> 00:06:46,370
Really, you guys do not need to throw me a going-away party.

144
00:06:46,370 --> 00:06:47,200
Are you kidding me?

145
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:49,930
How often can you say "bon voyage" to somebody

146
00:06:49,930 --> 00:06:53,210
when they're actually going on a voyage?

147
00:06:54,960 --> 00:06:56,370
Hello, Rajesh.

148
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:01,600
Hello, Amy. Nice to see you.

149
00:07:04,890 --> 00:07:07,710
What can I say? It's funnier with the accent.

150
00:07:08,570 --> 00:07:10,190
There's beer in the fridge.

151
00:07:10,190 --> 00:07:12,500
Anyway, you guys really don't need to make a big deal.

152
00:07:12,500 --> 00:07:14,140
Leonard, you're being selfish.

153
00:07:14,140 --> 00:07:17,500
We need to give you a proper send-off so we'll have closure

154
00:07:17,500 --> 00:07:20,300
when you die at sea and crabs eat your face.

155
00:07:21,380 --> 00:07:23,900
Sheldon, sweetie, shut up.

156
00:07:24,490 --> 00:07:25,400
You know, one of the things

157
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:26,840
that helped me get through Howard being in space

158
00:07:26,840 --> 00:07:29,580
for so long was getting married before he left.

159
00:07:33,510 --> 00:07:36,340
Bernadette, sweetie, shut up.

160
00:07:37,240 --> 00:07:37,890
Okay.

161
00:07:38,540 --> 00:07:39,950
I have a request to make.

162
00:07:39,950 --> 00:07:42,350
And now he can talk.

163
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:43,840
I want to cut open your brain

164
00:07:43,840 --> 00:07:46,170
and see what the heck's going on in there.

165
00:07:47,570 --> 00:07:51,180
The only person allowed inside this head is Dr. Phil.

166
00:07:52,370 --> 00:07:53,120
Anyway, I-

167
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:55,380
I spoke to my new lady friend about meeting you all,

168
00:07:55,380 --> 00:07:56,920
and she thought it would be easier for her

169
00:07:56,920 --> 00:07:58,410
to start with just one.

170
00:07:58,410 --> 00:07:59,890
Oh, gee, I don't know.

171
00:07:59,890 --> 00:08:02,150
My schedule's a little busy.

172
00:08:02,830 --> 00:08:04,820
Actually, I was thinking Leonard.

173
00:08:04,820 --> 00:08:07,770
Thank you, Raj. I'd be honored.

174
00:08:07,770 --> 00:08:08,440
What the hell?

175
00:08:08,440 --> 00:08:10,730
I thought I was your best friend.

176
00:08:11,110 --> 00:08:14,070
You are, but you've got kind of a big personality,

177
00:08:14,070 --> 00:08:18,230
with your flashy clothes and your Woody Allen swagger.

178
00:08:20,870 --> 00:08:23,740
You know, maybe she'd be more comfortable meeting a girl first.

179
00:08:23,740 --> 00:08:25,210
Good idea. Bernadette?

180
00:08:25,210 --> 00:08:27,030
What the hell?!

181
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:29,240
Well, you're very pretty.

182
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:31,030
That could be intimidating to another woman.

183
00:08:31,030 --> 00:08:32,710
Oh, yeah.

184
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:36,580
Hey, you don't think I'm pretty enough to scare your girlfriend?

185
00:08:36,920 --> 00:08:38,110
Calm down, Bernie.

186
00:08:38,110 --> 00:08:40,190
You're very scary.

187
00:08:41,890 --> 00:08:43,710
- It should be me. - Why?

188
00:08:43,710 --> 00:08:46,810
So you can make jokes about cutting open my brain?

189
00:08:46,810 --> 00:08:49,430
A, that was not a joke.

190
00:08:49,430 --> 00:08:51,420
That was a sincere request.

191
00:08:52,290 --> 00:08:54,060
And B, more importantly,

192
00:08:54,060 --> 00:08:55,850
I was the outsider to this group,

193
00:08:55,850 --> 00:08:58,190
and I know how frightening that can be.

194
00:08:58,190 --> 00:09:01,610
But you guys took me in and made me feel loved,

195
00:09:01,610 --> 00:09:03,770
like I was family.

196
00:09:06,470 --> 00:09:08,560
Fine, I'll do it.

197
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:13,110
So, after I started dating Sheldon,

198
00:09:13,110 --> 00:09:15,760
I met Leonard, and then everybody else,

199
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:17,950
and they've all been so wonderful to me.

200
00:09:17,950 --> 00:09:19,510
That's really nice to hear.

201
00:09:19,510 --> 00:09:21,930
Maybe next week, we could all get together.

202
00:09:21,930 --> 00:09:23,990
Oh, Lucy, you don't have to answer that.

203
00:09:23,990 --> 00:09:26,300
Don't put her on the spot. She hates that.

204
00:09:26,300 --> 00:09:26,890
Am I right?

205
00:09:26,890 --> 00:09:28,000
Tell her how much you hate being put on the spot.

206
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:30,230
Go ahead, tell her.

207
00:09:30,230 --> 00:09:31,280
Ignore him.

208
00:09:31,280 --> 00:09:33,200
He's a little nervous 'cause he doesn't think I understand

209
00:09:33,200 --> 00:09:34,990
the severity of your social anxiety.

210
00:09:34,990 --> 00:09:37,080
What the...? Are you crazy?

211
00:09:37,080 --> 00:09:38,150
You can't talk about social anxiety

212
00:09:38,150 --> 00:09:39,700
to someone who has social anxiety.

213
00:09:39,700 --> 00:09:41,900
It makes them socially anxious!

214
00:09:42,650 --> 00:09:44,700
Excuse me, but I'm a neurobiologist.

215
00:09:44,700 --> 00:09:46,230
I think I'm a little more qualified than you

216
00:09:46,230 --> 00:09:48,990
to understand what's not working in your girlfriend's brain!

217
00:09:50,060 --> 00:09:51,660
Don't call her my girlfriend.

218
00:09:51,660 --> 00:09:52,650
We haven't discussed whether or not

219
00:09:52,650 --> 00:09:54,690
we're girlfriend or boyfriend yet.

220
00:09:55,780 --> 00:09:57,640
Now that it's out there...

221
00:09:59,820 --> 00:10:01,110
...are you my girlfriend?

222
00:10:01,110 --> 00:10:02,110
By the way, if you say no,

223
00:10:02,110 --> 00:10:04,490
I'll never be happy again.

224
00:10:05,650 --> 00:10:07,580
Not to put you on the spot.

225
00:10:09,700 --> 00:10:12,000
I think I have to go to the bathroom.

226
00:10:16,020 --> 00:10:16,820
We might as well go ahead and eat.

227
00:10:16,820 --> 00:10:18,950
She's not coming back anytime soon.

228
00:10:25,540 --> 00:10:26,760
This is ridiculous.

229
00:10:26,760 --> 00:10:27,940
We're shopping for a party.

230
00:10:27,940 --> 00:10:30,040
This store doesn't even have a party section.

231
00:10:30,040 --> 00:10:32,440
Yeah, it does, and here we are.

232
00:10:34,380 --> 00:10:36,110
You know, I have to say, Penny,

233
00:10:36,110 --> 00:10:38,180
I don't understand why you of all people

234
00:10:38,180 --> 00:10:40,350
are encouraging Leonard to do this.

235
00:10:40,350 --> 00:10:43,160
Well, I'm his girlfriend; of course I'm gonna support him.

236
00:10:43,160 --> 00:10:45,730
Yeah, well, you're his girlfriend for now.

237
00:10:45,730 --> 00:10:47,160
You know, maybe you're not aware of this,

238
00:10:47,160 --> 00:10:48,860
but there is a rich tradition

239
00:10:48,860 --> 00:10:53,740
of men at sea finding comfort in each other's arms and britches.

240
00:10:55,750 --> 00:10:58,180
Honey, this is a big deal for Leonard, okay?

241
00:10:58,180 --> 00:10:59,740
He gets to work with Stephen Hawking.

242
00:10:59,740 --> 00:11:01,670
Who, by the way, will not be on the boat.

243
00:11:01,670 --> 00:11:02,840
I checked it out.

244
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:05,800
It's not that big of an opportunity.

245
00:11:05,800 --> 00:11:07,730
And even if Hawking's theories are correct,

246
00:11:07,730 --> 00:11:10,360
all they prove is where the universe came from,

247
00:11:10,360 --> 00:11:13,860
why everything exists and what its ultimate end will be.

248
00:11:13,860 --> 00:11:15,410
I mean, me?

249
00:11:15,410 --> 00:11:17,840
I'm interested in the big questions.

250
00:11:19,730 --> 00:11:23,380
Oh, my God, Sheldon the genius is jealous of Leonard.

251
00:11:23,380 --> 00:11:25,100
I'm not jealous.

252
00:11:25,100 --> 00:11:26,770
I'm just very unhappy

253
00:11:26,770 --> 00:11:27,970
that good things are happening for him

254
00:11:27,970 --> 00:11:30,080
and not happening for me.

255
00:11:30,680 --> 00:11:32,940
Look, sweetie, this is a natural thing to feel, okay?

256
00:11:32,940 --> 00:11:34,990
But just because good things are happening to Leonard

257
00:11:34,990 --> 00:11:36,860
doesn't take anything away from you.

258
00:11:36,860 --> 00:11:38,410
You know what? Let me tell you a little story.

259
00:11:38,410 --> 00:11:40,650
Once there was a girl who worked at the Cheesecake Factory,

260
00:11:40,650 --> 00:11:42,180
and she wasn't very good at her job.

261
00:11:42,180 --> 00:11:44,340
- It was you. - It wasn't me.

262
00:11:45,710 --> 00:11:47,240
But she was also an actress,

263
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:48,600
and we were both up for the same part

264
00:11:48,600 --> 00:11:49,820
in a toothpaste commercial.

265
00:11:49,820 --> 00:11:51,780
She got it. Look, I was so jealous.

266
00:11:51,780 --> 00:11:54,560
But instead of ripping out her fake blonde hair...

267
00:11:54,560 --> 00:11:56,480
You ripped out your own fake blonde hair.

268
00:11:56,480 --> 00:11:58,100
I...

269
00:11:58,530 --> 00:12:00,260
looked her in the eye,

270
00:12:00,260 --> 00:12:02,550
smiled and said, "I'm happy for you."

271
00:12:02,550 --> 00:12:04,620
Because that's what friends do.

272
00:12:05,480 --> 00:12:08,470
- They lie so they don't look petty. - Yeah.

273
00:12:09,190 --> 00:12:11,800
- How? - Like this.

274
00:12:12,060 --> 00:12:14,700
I am so happy for you.

275
00:12:19,270 --> 00:12:22,090
No wonder you didn't get that toothpaste commercial.

276
00:12:28,940 --> 00:12:30,700
I want to apologize for Amy last night.

277
00:12:30,700 --> 00:12:33,250
She was completely out of line.

278
00:12:39,210 --> 00:12:40,690
Are you... are you not speaking to me

279
00:12:40,690 --> 00:12:42,780
or did the screen freeze again?

280
00:12:42,780 --> 00:12:45,010
Amy wasn't the problem.

281
00:12:45,010 --> 00:12:46,670
Okay. I know.

282
00:12:47,320 --> 00:12:48,340
It was me.

283
00:12:48,340 --> 00:12:50,930
I-I pushed too hard. I'm sorry.

284
00:12:50,930 --> 00:12:52,410
Thank you.

285
00:12:53,140 --> 00:12:54,580
You know, I-I've been thinking that...

286
00:12:54,580 --> 00:12:58,310
maybe meeting somebody one-on-one is too intense,

287
00:12:58,310 --> 00:12:59,560
so...

288
00:12:59,560 --> 00:13:01,480
Friday night, my friends are having a party.

289
00:13:01,480 --> 00:13:03,470
- A party? - A little one!

290
00:13:03,470 --> 00:13:05,730
It's-it's a farewell for Leonard,

291
00:13:05,730 --> 00:13:08,250
so all the attention will be on him.

292
00:13:08,250 --> 00:13:10,550
If you wear something brown and sit on the couch,

293
00:13:10,550 --> 00:13:12,460
they won't even know you're there.

294
00:13:14,170 --> 00:13:15,530
I'm not sure.

295
00:13:15,530 --> 00:13:17,320
- Oh, please? - Raj.

296
00:13:17,320 --> 00:13:18,950
Come on. Don't make me beg.

297
00:13:18,950 --> 00:13:21,570
And I'm from India, so I know how to do it.

298
00:13:24,490 --> 00:13:26,220
Okay.

299
00:13:26,220 --> 00:13:27,340
Y... Thank you!

300
00:13:27,340 --> 00:13:28,860
Th-This means a lot to me.

301
00:13:28,860 --> 00:13:30,680
My friends are like my family.

302
00:13:31,260 --> 00:13:31,780
Unless you don't like them;

303
00:13:31,780 --> 00:13:33,940
in which case, they're dead to me.

304
00:13:37,190 --> 00:13:39,370
So, have you ever spent a long time on a boat before?

305
00:13:39,370 --> 00:13:40,910
- Yeah. - Are you referring to the time

306
00:13:40,910 --> 00:13:44,280
we got stuck on the Small World ride at Disneyland?

307
00:13:45,950 --> 00:13:47,450
Yeah.

308
00:13:50,270 --> 00:13:51,630
I'm proud of you, Leonard.

309
00:13:51,630 --> 00:13:54,340
Working out on the North Sea for months--

310
00:13:54,340 --> 00:13:56,750
- that's really something. - I know.

311
00:13:56,750 --> 00:13:58,180
As far as science goes,

312
00:13:58,180 --> 00:14:00,620
this is the adventure of a lifetime.

313
00:14:00,620 --> 00:14:02,010
Maybe your lifetime.

314
00:14:02,010 --> 00:14:03,870
I went to space.

315
00:14:06,180 --> 00:14:07,590
It's not a competition.

316
00:14:07,590 --> 00:14:09,080
You're right, you're right.

317
00:14:09,080 --> 00:14:10,490
I'm really proud of you, and...

318
00:14:10,490 --> 00:14:12,780
I'm gonna miss you when you're gone.

319
00:14:13,510 --> 00:14:15,520
And space beats water.

320
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:20,090
Rajesh, I thought Lucy was coming.

321
00:14:20,090 --> 00:14:22,720
She is. She's just running a little late.

322
00:14:22,720 --> 00:14:24,890
You know how it is-- girls always fussing about

323
00:14:24,890 --> 00:14:26,460
their hair, their makeup.

324
00:14:26,460 --> 00:14:27,670
She'll be here.

325
00:14:27,670 --> 00:14:29,530
Just give it a rest, okay?

326
00:14:32,010 --> 00:14:34,790
Um, can I have your attention, everyone?

327
00:14:37,110 --> 00:14:40,570
That's, uh, B-flat, for those who don't have perfect pitch.

328
00:14:41,500 --> 00:14:44,000
I would like to propose a toast

329
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:47,420
to my best friend, Dr. Leonard Hofstadter.

330
00:14:47,420 --> 00:14:51,140
He has been presented with a wonderful opportunity,

331
00:14:51,140 --> 00:14:54,360
and I couldn't be happier for him.

332
00:14:57,060 --> 00:14:58,280
Thank you, Sheldon.

333
00:14:58,280 --> 00:15:00,400
That must've been very hard for you to say.

334
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:02,280
Well, I mean it.

335
00:15:02,280 --> 00:15:04,000
I'm really happy for you.

336
00:15:04,940 --> 00:15:07,770
And that's how you get a toothpaste commercial. Cheers.

337
00:15:08,610 --> 00:15:10,340
Cheers.

338
00:15:12,080 --> 00:15:15,580
It was really nice of you to try to be happy for Leonard.

339
00:15:15,580 --> 00:15:16,640
Thank you.

340
00:15:17,080 --> 00:15:19,190
It must've killed you when I went to space.

341
00:15:23,340 --> 00:15:25,040
Oh, no.

342
00:15:25,040 --> 00:15:27,260
Buddy, you okay?

343
00:15:29,870 --> 00:15:31,240
Oh, man.

344
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:32,910
What's going on?

345
00:15:33,520 --> 00:15:35,730
Uh, go ahead. Read it.

346
00:15:35,730 --> 00:15:37,930
"Raj, I can't come to the party.

347
00:15:37,940 --> 00:15:40,940
This is all just too much for me.

348
00:15:40,940 --> 00:15:44,880
I don't think we should see each other anymore.

349
00:15:44,880 --> 00:15:47,170
Sorry. Lucy."

350
00:15:48,710 --> 00:15:49,940
Excuse me.

351
00:15:49,940 --> 00:15:52,090
Raj, I'm so sorry.

352
00:15:52,090 --> 00:15:53,590
Me, too.

353
00:15:57,290 --> 00:16:00,190
It did not kill me when you went to space.

354
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:06,350
Monkeys went to space.

355
00:16:10,970 --> 00:16:12,470
Well, here we are.

356
00:16:12,470 --> 00:16:14,270
Yep.

357
00:16:14,650 --> 00:16:16,020
I'm really gonna miss you.

358
00:16:16,020 --> 00:16:17,970
I'm gonna miss you, too.

359
00:16:17,970 --> 00:16:20,410
Penny, we're in the red zone.

360
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:24,020
The white zone is for loading and unloading.

361
00:16:24,020 --> 00:16:26,280
We're breaking the law.

362
00:16:26,700 --> 00:16:29,110
- Okay, there's no space in the white zone, so... - Anyway,

363
00:16:30,460 --> 00:16:32,880
we can E-mail, and I-I think the phone connections

364
00:16:32,880 --> 00:16:33,790
are pretty good.

365
00:16:33,790 --> 00:16:34,950
All right, you have to get out of the car right now.

366
00:16:34,950 --> 00:16:36,870
I'm not going to jail for you.

367
00:16:36,870 --> 00:16:38,250
Would you just relax?

368
00:16:38,250 --> 00:16:39,780
Oh, I see a space in the white zone.

369
00:16:39,780 --> 00:16:41,990
Quick, circle the airport.

370
00:16:43,010 --> 00:16:44,600
Did you bring enough inhalers?

371
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:45,340
Yeah.

372
00:16:45,340 --> 00:16:46,860
And, uh, extra Dramamine?

373
00:16:46,860 --> 00:16:49,450
You remember what happened on It's a Small World.

374
00:16:50,520 --> 00:16:51,870
- I'm covered. - Okay.

375
00:16:51,870 --> 00:16:54,260
Oh, dear Lord, a police officer's

376
00:16:54,260 --> 00:16:55,510
glancing in our direction.

377
00:16:55,510 --> 00:16:56,670
We've been made.

378
00:16:58,630 --> 00:17:00,630
Calm down. I'm getting out.

379
00:17:01,260 --> 00:17:03,010
I have something I want to give you.

380
00:17:03,010 --> 00:17:03,920
Oh, Leonard.

381
00:17:03,920 --> 00:17:05,040
It's just a heart-shaped locket with a picture of

382
00:17:05,040 --> 00:17:06,780
Leonard's face in it. He got it at the mall on clearance.

383
00:17:06,780 --> 00:17:08,500
Now move, move, move!

384
00:17:11,120 --> 00:17:12,840
I love you.

385
00:17:13,490 --> 00:17:15,070
I love you, too.

386
00:17:17,760 --> 00:17:18,970
Don't worry, Officer.

387
00:17:18,970 --> 00:17:20,510
They just love each other.

388
00:17:20,510 --> 00:17:23,170
We're not smuggling drugs.

389
00:17:30,340 --> 00:17:31,310
Raj, it's Penny.

390
00:17:31,310 --> 00:17:33,030
Are you in there?

391
00:17:33,030 --> 00:17:34,640
Hang on.

392
00:17:37,030 --> 00:17:38,900
Hey. I'm just coming back from the airport.

393
00:17:38,900 --> 00:17:40,720
I wanted to see how you're doing.

394
00:17:40,720 --> 00:17:42,350
That's-that's very nice of you.

395
00:17:42,350 --> 00:17:44,510
Uh, come, come. Come on in.

396
00:17:44,510 --> 00:17:45,810
Can't stay long.

397
00:17:45,810 --> 00:17:48,960
I left Sheldon in the car with the window cracked open.

398
00:17:50,850 --> 00:17:52,820
He's gonna go through that activity book

399
00:17:52,820 --> 00:17:55,230
in, like, 30 seconds, so...

400
00:17:56,440 --> 00:17:58,140
Are you okay?

401
00:17:59,790 --> 00:18:00,890
No.

402
00:18:02,780 --> 00:18:04,950
I'm so sorry.

403
00:18:04,950 --> 00:18:06,080
No.

404
00:18:06,080 --> 00:18:07,830
It's my fault.

405
00:18:07,840 --> 00:18:10,890
You know, I finally found someone who was right for me,

406
00:18:10,890 --> 00:18:13,520
and I-I drove her away.

407
00:18:13,530 --> 00:18:16,930
Oh, Raj.

408
00:18:16,930 --> 00:18:19,010
Penny, I...

409
00:18:19,010 --> 00:18:21,060
I miss her already.

410
00:18:21,070 --> 00:18:22,530
I know how you feel.

411
00:18:22,530 --> 00:18:23,780
I miss Leonard, too.

412
00:18:23,790 --> 00:18:27,140
What's... what is wrong with me?

413
00:18:27,140 --> 00:18:30,020
Why-why can't I ever have love?

414
00:18:30,030 --> 00:18:30,720
You will.

415
00:18:30,720 --> 00:18:33,070
No, I... I won't.

416
00:18:33,070 --> 00:18:35,380
I'm-I'm unlovable.

417
00:18:35,380 --> 00:18:37,830
That's just the booze talking.

418
00:18:37,830 --> 00:18:39,650
No, it's not.

419
00:18:39,650 --> 00:18:42,370
I haven't had a drink since last night.

420
00:18:51,210 --> 00:18:54,330
- You're talking to me. - I am.

421
00:18:55,970 --> 00:18:58,640
And now I'm crying for a whole different reason!

422
00:18:58,640 --> 00:19:00,190
Me, too!

423
00:19:06,060 --> 00:19:07,680
So I-I guess what I'm saying is.

424
00:19:07,710 --> 00:19:09,580
I get where Lucy's coming from.

425
00:19:09,580 --> 00:19:11,330
That's great. Do you want some wine?

426
00:19:11,330 --> 00:19:12,780
Uh, no, water's fine.

427
00:19:12,780 --> 00:19:15,550
Anyhow, I-I've been thinking about it a lot,

428
00:19:15,550 --> 00:19:18,500
and-and I totally see why Lucy did what she did.

429
00:19:18,500 --> 00:19:19,420
I pushed too hard.

430
00:19:19,420 --> 00:19:21,440
But you know what? If I back off and give her enough space,

431
00:19:21,440 --> 00:19:23,590
maybe there's still a future for us.

432
00:19:23,590 --> 00:19:25,450
Yeah, the funny thing about life is that,

433
00:19:25,450 --> 00:19:27,350
you know, sometimes...

434
00:19:27,350 --> 00:19:29,840
Does he ever shut up?

435
00:19:30,200 --> 00:19:31,550
And then, it turns good again,

436
00:19:31,550 --> 00:19:34,830
that means it better than if never been bad for a while,

437
00:19:34,830 --> 00:19:37,020
and now, things are going...

438
00:19:37,020 --> 00:19:39,830
in fact, are very very bad.

439
00:19:39,830 --> 00:19:41,960
But at least my heart is starting to heal.

440
00:19:41,960 --> 00:19:43,620
Slowly but surely.

441
00:19:43,620 --> 00:19:45,870
And how I cried.

442
00:19:45,870 --> 00:19:48,900
It was like a little, uh, thunderstorm on my face.

443
00:19:48,900 --> 00:19:50,270
But I'm a man, okay?

444
00:19:50,270 --> 00:19:52,450
So I need to pull myself together, pick up a pen

445
00:19:52,450 --> 00:19:54,060
and get it all out in my journal.

446
00:19:54,060 --> 00:19:56,370
I mean, it's not all bad, right?

447
00:19:56,370 --> 00:19:57,550
Having my heart broken

448
00:19:57,550 --> 00:19:59,300
has allowed me to finally speak in front of you...

449
00:19:59,300 --> 00:20:01,500
so, you know, it was a silver lining.

